My solution is similar to @**a1267ab**'s but I'll add slightly more details.

Let  $(x_n)_{n>0},(y_n)_{n>0}$  be sequences defined by  $x_n=a_n/n$  and  $y_n=b_n/n$  for all  $n\geqslant 1$ .
We'll work on  $(x_n)$  only as similar result can be applied to  $(y_n)$ . Note that we want to show  $x_{1010}=y_{1009}$ .

Let  $T(x)=\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}{x_nx^n}$ . From the recurrence relation, we have  $T'(x)-1=2018T(x)+x^2T'(x).$ So, setting  $P(x)=T(x)+\frac{1}{2018}$ , we get  $2018P(x)=P'(x)(1-x^2)$ .
Similarly, if we let  $Q(x)=\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}{y_nx^n}+\frac{1}{2020}$ , we will get  $2020Q(x)=Q'(x)(1-x^2)$ .

Now, let  $R(x)$  be the solution to  $R(x)=R'(x)(1-x^2)$  with  $R(0)=1$ .
Easy to see that  $P(x)=R(x)^{2018}/2018$  and  $Q(x)=R(x)^{2020}/2020$ .
So we'll solve for  $R(x)$ . We have
\begin{align*}
& \frac{R'(x)}{R(x)}=\frac{1}{1-x^2}
\implies & \int \frac{R'(x)}{R(x)}dx = \frac{1}{2}\int \left( \frac{1}{1+x}+\frac{1}{1-x}\right) dx
\implies & \log (R(x))=\frac{1}{2} (\log (1+x)-\log (1-x)) +c_1
\implies & R(x)=c_2(1+x)^{1/2}(1-x)^{-1/2}.
\end{align*}
From  $R(0)=1$ , we conclude that  $R(x)=(1+x)^{1/2}(1-x)^{-1/2}$ .

Hence, we have
\begin{align*}
x_{1010} & =[x^{1010}]P(x)
& =\frac{1}{2018}[x^{1010}]\left( (1+x)^{1009}(1-x)^{-1009}\right) 
& =\frac{1}{2018}[x^{1010}] \sum_{k=0}^{1009}{\binom{1009}{k}x^k}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}{\binom{k+1008}{1008}x^k} 
& =\frac{1}{2018}\left( 0+ \sum_{k=0}^{1009}{\binom{1009}{k}\binom{(1010-k)+1008}{1008}}\right) 
& =\frac{1}{2018}\sum_{k=0}^{1009}{\binom{1009}{k}\binom{2018-k}{1008}}
& = \sum_{k=0}^{1009}{\frac{(2018-k)!}{2\cdot k!\cdot (1009-k)!\cdot (1010-k)!}}
\end{align*}
and
\begin{align*}
y_{1009} & =[x^{1009}]Q(x)
& =\frac{1}{2020}[x^{1009}]\left( (1+x)^{1010}(1-x)^{-1010}\right) 
& =\frac{1}{2020}[x^{1009}] \sum_{k=0}^{1010}{\binom{1010}{k}x^k}\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}{\binom{k+1009}{1009}x^k} 
& =\frac{1}{2020}\sum_{k=0}^{1009}{\binom{1010}{k}\binom{2018-k}{1009}}
& = \sum_{k=0}^{1009}{\frac{(2018-k)!}{2\cdot k!\cdot (1010-k)!\cdot (1009-k)!}}
& = x_{1010}. \quad \blacksquare
\end{align*}

