In typical ``American geometry" fashion, we now prove many lemmas.**<span style="color:#ff9a00">Claim 1.</span>** Quadrilateral  $AM_AB_1C_1$  is cyclic.

*<span style="color:#ff9a00">Proof. </span>*Take the spiral similarity at  $M_A$  sending  $BC_1 \to CB_1$ , which is actually a rotation as  $BC_1 = CB_1$ . So  $BM_A = CM_A$  and the result follows.  $\square$ **<span style="color:#ff9a00">Claim 2 (EGMO TST 2019/5).</span>** Circle  $(AB_1A_1C_1)$  has diameter. In addition,  $B_1, I, C_1$  are collinear.

