Now, we note that   $$ (B,P;I_1, I_2)=(C,Q;I_3,I_4) = -1\text{ (equal cross ratios). } $$  Since  $B, P$  are the exsimilicenter and insimilicenter of incircles of  $\triangle ABK$ ,  $\triangle ABL$ , and  $I_1, I_2$  their centers, and similar thing for  $C, Q, I_3, I_4$ , hence  $BC, I_1I_3, I_2I_4$  concur at  $U$ ; also,  $PQ$  passes through  $U$  due to Prism Lemma.

