<blockquote>Let  $ABC$  be an acute triangle with circumcircle  $\Omega$  and orthocenter  $H$ . Points  $D$  and  $E$  lie on segments  $AB$  and  $AC$  respectively, such that  $AD = AE$ . The lines through  $B$  and  $C$  parallel to  $\overline{DE}$  intersect  $\Omega$  again at  $P$  and  $Q$ , respectively. Denote by  $\omega$  the circumcircle of  $\triangle ADE$ . 
