For the part (b), Let  $J$  is the reflection of  $H$  wrt  $AC$ . We claim that the points  $J,E,Q$  are collinear. For the proof,
\begin{eqnarray*}
\angle AJE=\angle AHE=\angle ADE=\angle AED=\angle ACQ=\angle AJQ.
\end{eqnarray*}
Which follows that points  $J,R,Q$  are collinear. Similarly the points  $P,D,K$  are also collinear.  $\square$ Since line  $BP\parallel CQ$ , therefore  $\angle BJQ=\angle CBP$ . Let  $EQ\cap DP=G$ . Now,
\begin{eqnarray*}
\angle HEG=2\angle HJG=2\angle HKG=\angle HDG.
\end{eqnarray*}
So points  $H,D,E,G$  are cyclic.  $\square$

