From earlier,  $\measuredangle CPB = \measuredangle BDA$ , so  $APLD$  is cyclic. Likewise,  $BPKC$  is cyclic.

Now the quadrilateral  $AKLB$  is also cyclic, because
\[\measuredangle AKB = \measuredangle AKP + \measuredangle PKB = \measuredangle CBP + \measuredangle PCB = \measuredangle CPB\]
and similarly  $\measuredangle ALB = \measuredangle APD$ .

Now by Reim's theorem,  $\overline{CD} \parallel \overline{KL}$ . Thus  $CDKL$  is a trapezoid whose legs intersect at  $P$  and whose diagonals intersect at  $E$ , so line  $PE$  bisects the bases  $\overline{CD}$  and  $\overline{KL}$ , as desired.</details>

