Denote by  $ \sigma (n) := $  sum of divisors of  $n$ .
WLOG let  $ 1 = d_1 < d_2 < \dots < d_m = n $ \begin{align*} \sigma (n)^2  & = \left( \sum_{i=1}^m d_i \right)^2   & = \left( 1 + n + \sum_{i=2}^{m-1} d_i \right)^2 
& = 1 + n^2 + \left( \sum_{i=2}^{m-1} d_i \right)^2 + 2n + \left( 2 \sum_{i=1}^{m-1} d_i  \right) (n+1)  & = 1 + n^2 + \left( \sum_{i=2}^{m-1} d_i \right) \left( \sum_{i=2}^{m-1} \frac{n}{d_i} \right) + 2n + \left( 2 \sum_{i=1}^{m-1} d_i \right) (n+1 )  & \geq 1 + n^2 +\left( \sum_{i=2}^{m-1} \sqrt{n} \right)^2 + 2n + \left( 2 \sum_{i=1}^{m-1} 2 \right) (n+1)  & = 1 +n^2 + (m-2)^2n + 2n + 4(m-2)(n+1) \end{align*}

\begin{align*} \therefore \frac{ \sigma (n)^2 }{ m^2 } & \geq \frac{1}{m^2} \left( 1 +n^2 + (m-2)^2n + 2n + 4(m-2)(n+1) \right)  & = \frac{1}{m^2} \left( -7 + n^2 -2n + 4m \right) + n \end{align*}

To show :  $ 4(-7 + n^2 -2n +4m ) \geq m^2 $  $ \Leftrightarrow -28 + 4n^2 - 8n + 16m \geq m^2 $  $ \Leftrightarrow ( 4n^2 - 8n + 4 ) + 32 \geq ( m^2 - 16m + 64 ) $  $ \leftrightarrow 4(n-1)^2+ 32 \geq (m-8)^2 $ Now observe that for  $ n > 2 $  we have  $ n-1 \geq m ( \because \phi(n) \geq 2 \ \forall \ n > 2 \ )$  $ \therefore 4(n-1)^2 + 32 \geq 4m^2 + 32 $ **<span style="color:#00f">Claim : </span>** $ 4m^2 + 32 > m^2 - 16m + 64 $  $ \Leftrightarrow 3m^2 + 16m - 32 > 0 $ Now the function  $ f(m) = 3m^2 + 16m -32 $  is increasing for all positive  $m$  
and observe that  $ \forall \ m \geq  2 $  we have  $ f(m) > 0 $   $ \therefore \frac{\sigma (n)}{m} > \sqrt{ n + \frac{1}{4}} \ \forall \ n > 2 $ And clearly for  $ n = 2 $  we get  $ \frac{ \sigma (2) }{2} = \frac{3}{2} = \sqrt{ 2 + \frac{1}{4} } $ Thus we have equality only for  $ n = 2 $ . $ \therefore \frac{ d_1 + d_2 + \dots + d_m }{m} \geq \sqrt{ n + \frac{1}{4} } \ \forall \ n \geq 2 $ Hence, proved.

