Therefore:   $$ S(\triangle MEF) = \frac{a(s-a)}{2bc} \cdot S(\triangle ABC) = \frac{a(s-a)}{2bc} \cdot \frac{bc \sin 2\alpha}{2} = \frac{(s-a)a \cdot \sin \alpha \cdot \cos \alpha}{2} $$  On another hand:   $$ S(\triangle MEF) = \frac{EF \cdot MZ}{2}=\frac{2(s-a) \cdot \sin \alpha \cdot MZ}{2} =(s-a) \cdot \sin \alpha \cdot MZ $$  We conclude that:   $$ (s-a) \cdot sin \alpha \cdot MZ = \frac{(s-a)a \cdot \sin \alpha \cdot \cos \alpha}{2} \implies MZ = 0,5a \cos \alpha = BM \cos \alpha =MY=MZ $$  And we are done !

