Let  $\alpha=\angle PXO_1$ , we claim that  $\angle O_1PA=\angle O_1AP=\alpha$ .

Firstly note that the reflection of  $P$  over  $x$  lies on  $\omega_3$ , because the center of  $\omega_3$ ,  $C$  lies on  $x$ .
We have
\begin{align*}
    \angle O_1AP'&=\angle O_1AP-\angle P'AP&=180^\circ-\angle PXO_1-2\angle XAP&=180^\circ-\angle PXO_1-\angle XO_2P&=\angle O_1O_2P-\angle PXO_1&=2\angle PXO_1-\angle PXO_1&=\alpha
\end{align*}
and
